  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nIssued at 215 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe northwest flow pattern remains in place aloft into the\nweekend and next week, with a larger upper level ridge building\nacross the Plains and intermountain west this weekend. This\nallows heat to build beneath the ridge with the thermal ridge\nbuilding eastward toward Sunday into Monday. Return flow off the\ngulf into the region sends dewpoints back into the 70s along\nwith ensembles showing a trend of higher than average moisture\nand temperatures across the area for this time period, matching\nthe trend the past few days of heat and humidity concerns\nincreasing for the Sunday and Monday time period. Latest heat\nindex values near and above 100 for Sunday and Monday. \n\nSome dampening of the ridge across the area later Sunday into\nnext week, with ripples in the ridge, and increasing chance for\nthunderstorms Sunday night into Monday night with waves topping\nand traveling southeastward through the upper ridge. This\npattern sets up a ring of fire situation with ensembles trying\nto bring a storm complex through the area late Sunday night and\nMonday morning. The area is outlooked for severe possibilities\nin Day 4 and 5 for this possibility. The upper ridge then\namplifies a bit more across the west into the latter portion of\nthe week, with more troughing toward the MS Valley region into\nthe Great Lakes suggesting additional precipitation chances or\nstorm chances into the end of the forecast period.",
